# Twenty4Seven redesign rules
Goal: Apple Music-level polish. Simple on the surface, many features underneath.

## Non-negotiables
- Keep the existing brand palette from docs/CURRENT-TOKENS.md. Do not invent new colors. Derive tints/shades from it only.
- Never remove a feature in docs/FEATURES.md. Redesign how it is presented, not whether it exists.
- Progressive disclosure: one primary action per screen, secondary features behind menus, sheets, or long-press.
- Max 4-5 tabs. Everything else is reachable from Home or Search.

## Use real iOS components, never imitations
- Tabs: expo-router native tabs. No custom tab bar.
- Headers: native large titles that collapse. No hand-rolled headers.
- Sheets: native form sheets with detents. No custom bottom-sheet libs unless unavoidable.
- Icons: SF Symbols via expo-symbols only. No emoji, no mixed icon sets.
- Menus: native context menus on long-press.
- Liquid Glass only on chrome (tab bar, floating controls, mini-player), never on content. Always check availability and fall back to expo-blur.
- Haptics (expo-haptics) on every meaningful tap and toggle.

## Anti-slop
- No stacks of white rounded cards with shadows. Prefer full-bleed lists, grouped sections, and big imagery/type.
- No gradient buttons. No centered-everything layouts. No "Welcome back 👋" copy.
- Every screen needs loading, empty, and error states.
- Every color via theme tokens with light and dark values. No hex codes in components.
- Every spacing/radius/font size via tokens. No magic numbers.
- Respect safe areas and Dynamic Type.
- Animations: Reanimated springs, never linear timing for UI movement.
